            "type": "text",
            "text": "Based on your saved memory file (`/topics/entertainment.md`), you follow director **Denis Villeneuve** (and enjoy science fiction films). \n\nDepending on whether you mean the **most recent film project he was announced to direct** or his **next upcoming theatrical release**, here are the details for both:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Latest Newly Announced Project: The Next *James Bond* Film (*Bond 26*)\n* **Summary:** On June 25, 2025, Amazon MGM Studios officially announced that Denis Villeneuve will direct the 26th installment in the *James Bond* franchise—the first film under Amazon MGM's creative control following Daniel Craig's departure. *Peaky Blinders* creator Steven Knight is writing the screenplay, with Amy Pascal and David Heyman serving as producers and Tanya Lapointe as executive producer. Final screen tests to cast the new 007 have been underway in late 2026—Villeneuve even jokingly teased a reveal at the LACMA Art+Film Gala on November 7, 2026—with Robert Pattinson, Callum Turner, Jack Lowden, Josh O'Connor, and Nicholas Hoult reported among the contenders.\n* **Release Date:** **No official exact release date yet** (expected **2028**, with production reportedly slated to begin in 2027 after Villeneuve finishes his *Dune: Part Three* obligations).\n* **Source URL:** https://deadline.com/2025/06/denis-villeneuve-james-bond-amazon-mgm-studios-1236442917/\n\n---\n\n### 2. Next Upcoming Release (Sci-Fi): *Dune: Part Three*\n* **Summary:** Since you enjoy science fiction, Villeneuve's immediate upcoming film is ***Dune: Part Three***, the conclusion to his *Dune* trilogy adapted from Frank Herbert's novel *Dune Messiah* and co-written with Brian K. Vaughan. Set nearly two decades after *Dune: Part Two*, the story follows Emperor Paul Atreides (Timothée Chalamet) as he faces political conspiracy, rebellion, and the consequences of his rule. Returning cast members Zendaya, Florence Pugh, Rebecca Ferguson, Jason Momoa, Javier Bardem, Charlotte Rampling, and Anya Taylor-Joy are joined by newcomers Robert Pattinson (as Scytale) and Isaach de Bankolé. The final trailer and IMAX 70mm advance tickets have already launched ahead of next month's premiere.\n* **Release Date:** **December 18, 2026** (simultaneous release in the United States and Japan as 『デューン 砂の惑星PART3』, with early openings on December 16 in select markets like the UK and South Korea).\n* **Source URLs:** \n  * Official Japan Site: https://dune-movie-3.jp/\n  * Deadline Coverage: https://deadline.com/2026/10/dune-part-three-smashes-bfi-imax-record-ticket-sales-1237169586/",
